      "marks_unanswered": 0,
      "question_text": "p-value of 0.03 means?",
      "options": {
        "A": "3% chance the alternative hypothesis is true",
        "B": "3% probability of observed results if null hypothesis were true",
        "C": "97% confidence in result",
        "D": "Effect size is large"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "p-value: probability of obtaining results at least as extreme as observed IF null hypothesis were true. p<0.05 = statistically significant (reject null). Does NOT measure effect size."
